swbrd-dtls-proxy
================

/usr/share/swbrd/key.pem is the deterministic-certificate signing key, seeded
into /var/lib/swbrd/key.pem on first install and never overwritten afterwards.

It is *deliberately public*.  The whole point of the deter scheme is that every
client derives the same certificate for a given half-year without any prior
exchange, which it can only do if the key is known.  Treat it as a protocol
constant, not as a secret; it authenticates nothing.

The plaintext side forwards to the host's SCTP-over-UDP endpoint (see -e in
/etc/default/swbrd-dtls-proxy).  That port is configured by net.sctp.udp_port,
which belongs to the swbrd VPN daemon and is not shipped by this package.
